# --- Bucket B: standard objects that already exist in the org, with ZERO DPEG customization ---
# (verified 0 custom __c fields and no DPEG-named listViews/webLinks in each dir)
# Account NARROWED 2026-08-10 (Task 1 fix round 2): the blanket ignore was silently dropping the
# entire objects/Account/** tree - including the two new record types (Broker_Firm,
# Investor_Entity) - from EVERY deploy attempt with zero error or warning. A check-only dry-run
# against usman-dpeg reported "no RecordType named Account.Broker_Firm found" for two
# PermissionSets, which read like fallout from the Lead/Contact failures in the same run but was
# not - it was this ignore rule, reproducible with Account alone in an otherwise-clean deploy
# ("No local changes to deploy" - zero files, zero errors, nothing to fix by editing Account's
# own metadata). The Bucket B rationale ("ZERO DPEG customization") stopped being true the moment
# Task 1 added two record types under Account/recordTypes/.
# ⚠ TWO FAILED ATTEMPTS BEFORE THIS ONE, BOTH INSTRUCTIVE. (1) Removing the Account/** line
# outright was too broad: Account/fields/** in this repo already contains multiple pre-existing,
# broken standard-field declarations unrelated to this task (ChannelProgramLevelName,
# ChannelProgramName, CleanStatus, DandbCompanyId, DunsNumber, IsCustomerPortal, IsPartner,
# NaicsCode, NaicsDesc, Tradestyle, YearStarted - ten "Could not resolve standard field's name"
# plus one custom-suffix error), almost certainly D&B/Data.com-era fields not resolvable in this
# org's edition/feature set. (2) Keeping `Account/**` and adding `!Account/recordTypes/**` (a
# gitignore-style negation) did NOT work - `force-app/main/default/objects/Account/**` prunes the
# `recordTypes` directory NODE itself, and per gitignore semantics a negation cannot re-include a
# path whose parent directory was already excluded; the negated recordTypes files simply never
# appeared in the deploy's file list, with no error at all (confirmed via the dry-run's own
# `files` array, not assumed). The fix below sidesteps negation entirely: ignore ONLY the known-
# broken `fields/**` subfolder directly, and leave `Account/Account.object-meta.xml` and
# `Account/recordTypes/**` un-ignored by simply never matching them - Account has no other
# subfolders today (verified: `fields/` and `recordTypes/` are the only two). Do not widen this
# to a blanket `Account/**` again without first resolving the eleven field-level errors above,
# and do not assume `!`-negation will rescue a path buried under a `dir/**` ignore elsewhere in
# this file without re-testing against a live dry-run first.
force-app/main/default/objects/Account/fields/**
force-app/main/default/objects/Asset/**
force-app/main/default/objects/Campaign/**
force-app/main/default/objects/Case/**
force-app/main/default/objects/CommSubscriptionChannelType/**
force-app/main/default/objects/Entitlement/**
force-app/main/default/objects/Location/**
force-app/main/default/objects/Product2/**
force-app/main/default/objects/ProductTransfer/**
force-app/main/default/objects/Shipment/**
force-app/main/default/objects/ShipmentItem/**
force-app/main/default/objects/TimeSlot/**
force-app/main/default/objects/WorkOrder/**
force-app/main/default/objects/WorkOrderLineItem/**
force-app/main/default/objects/WorkPlan/**
force-app/main/default/objects/WorkPlanTemplate/**
force-app/main/default/objects/OperatingHours/**

